  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Deal: Each player receives seven tiles.\n2. Opening: The player with the double-six sets it in the center. Players in turn (clockwise) must play a tile in the sixes suit onto the double-six until four arms are started.\n3. Play: Once all four arms are started, each player may add a tile to the end of any arm. Doubles are played across the line and do not branch. Unable to play: pass (turn passes).\n4. Scoring: If a player dominoes, they score the total pips in opponents' hands. If the game blocks, the player with the lowest pip total wins and scores (sum of others' pips minus own). Game is played to 60 points.",
    Player: "1. Deal: Each player receives seven tiles.\n2. Opening: The player with the double-six sets it in the center. Players in turn (clockwise) must play a tile in the sixes suit onto the double-six until four arms are started.\n3. Play: Once all four arms are started, each player may add a tile to the end of any arm. Doubles are played across the line and do not branch. Unable to play: pass (turn passes).\n4. Scoring: If a player dominoes, they score the total pips in opponents' hands. If the game blocks, the player with the lowest pip total wins and scores (sum of others' pips minus own). Game is played to 60 points.",
    objective: 'Be the first to play all your tiles (domino), or have the lowest pip total if the game blocks. First player to reach 60 points wins.',
    gameplay: "1. Deal: Each player receives seven tiles.\n2. Opening: The player with the double-six sets it in the center. Players in turn (clockwise) must play a tile in the sixes suit onto the double-six until four arms are started.\n3. Play: Once all four arms are started, each player may add a tile to the end of any arm. Doubles are played across the line and do not branch. Unable to play: pass (turn passes).\n4. Scoring: If a player dominoes, they score the total pips in opponents' hands. If the game blocks, the player with the lowest pip total wins and scores (sum of others' pips minus own). Game is played to 60 points.",
    keyRules: [
      'Player with the double-six starts; four arms of the spinner must be started before free play on any arm',
      "Score is pips in opponents' hands when you domino; blocked game: lowest hand wins and scores",
      'First to 60 points wins the game',
